  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Issues**\n\nI\'m starting to zero in on the user\'s frustration. The preview is broken, plagued by rate limits (429s), CORS and WebSocket connection issues, and some 404s on uploaded files. I need to figure out what changed recently to understand these errors.\n\n\n**Investigating the Cause**\n\nI\'ve got a clearer picture of the problem now. The `vite build && vite preview` command in the `package.json`\'s \"dev\" script is the culprit. The previous turn incorrectly switched the environment variable check and disabled HMR. This means the dev server is now *always* running a build and then previewing. I\'m focusing on why this major alteration happened and the implications for rate limits and connection loops. This constant build-preview cycle is probably slamming the API.\n\n\n**Pinpointing the Root Cause**\n\nI\'ve got it! The user\'s dev setup, specifically `vite preview`, causes the browser to individually request numerous source files when it should have built the target. This leads to a flood of requests, triggering a `429` error in the proxy or Google\'s frontend due to excessive rapid file loading. Those `WebSocket` errors are probably related to the rate-limit too.\n\n\n**Confirming the Solution**\n\nOkay, the lightbulb just went off! The root cause isn\'t just the individual file requests; it\'s also the *lack* of bundling. If the dev server is configured correctly, it serves the bundled code, preventing the flood of requests. So, the original intention to build and preview, if implemented correctly, should resolve the 429 errors. I need to verify why the user still encountered issues after this build process was implemented, though!\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will inspect the `package.json` file to understand the current configuration for build and dev scripts. This will help us determine how to optimize the build and preview configuration, so we bypass the browser\'s 429 Too Many Requests issue and resolve the 404 and WebSocket errors in the preview environment."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 5
      nanos: 755616183
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
